   "thumb": "You standing on the cashout box while everything burns, white border.",
   "script": "RUNTIME TARGET  7 to 8 minutes, six chapters, roughly a chapter a minute.\nThe joke is the format. Every chapter opens like a real guide and then tells the truth. Chapter four stops being a joke on purpose, which is what makes the rest of it land.\n\nCOLD OPEN  0:00 to 0:25\nFootage: a clean whiff, then a cashout held anyway.\n  \"Every Medium guide starts the same way. Some guy with four thousand hours tells you to hold an angle and control the lane.\"\n  \"I have sixty hours and I have never controlled anything in my life. So here is the version for us.\"\n\nCHAPTER 1, THE LOADOUT  0:25 to 1:40\n  \"Model 1887, defibrillator, and whatever gadget makes you laugh. That is the build.\"\n  \"The pros will tell you to run the meta. The meta assumes you can aim. We are building around the thing you can actually do, which is stand near a box and be extremely annoying.\"\nThen the real tip, said straight:\n  \"One honest bit of advice. If you are playing with randoms, take the healing beam. The fastest way to be useful when you are not good is to keep alive the person who is.\"\nSPOKEN SUBSCRIBE ASK lands here, around 1:00, plainly, over gameplay.\n\nCHAPTER 2, THE FIRST TEN SECONDS  1:40 to 2:50\n  \"Real guides say rotate to the contested cashout. Here is what actually happens to us. You land, you get lost, you hear fighting, you run towards the fighting, and you die to someone you never saw.\"\n  \"So do not go to the fight. Go to the box.\"\n  \"Whoever survives the fight has to come to you. Now the fight is in your room, and your room is the only place you have ever won anything.\"\n\nCHAPTER 3, HOW TO WIN A FIGHT  2:50 to 4:00\n  \"You are not going to win the duel. Accept that now, it will save you a season.\"\n  \"The good news is that this is not a duel game. It is a building game.\"\n  \"Shoot the floor. Shoot the wall. Take the stairs away. You do not have to beat him, you have to make the room worse for him than it is for you.\"\nBRAIN PAUSE here: freeze the frame mid fight, dip the game audio, explain what is actually happening, then unpause.\n\nCHAPTER 4, THE CASHOUT  4:00 to 5:30\nTone shift. Play this one straight, no jokes.\n  \"This is the part of the video that is not a joke.\"\n  \"Objective score is the stat nobody looks at, and it is the one that decides games.\"\n  \"I had a night where I got thirteen eliminations and came third. The same week I got three eliminations, died six times, and won twenty thousand.\"\n  \"Same weapon. Same player. The only thing that changed was where I was standing.\"\n\nCHAPTER 5, ADVANCED TECH  5:30 to 6:30\n  \"Advanced tech section. Here it is in full.\"\n  \"Gas, then fire.\"\n  \"Put the gas on the box, set it on fire, and stand behind it. It is not clever, it took me no skill to learn, and it works on people who are much better than me.\"\nFootage: the barrel throw and the thirteen second hold from the Fortune Stadium win.\n\nCHAPTER 6, RANKED MINDSET  6:30 to 7:30\n  \"Last one. You are going to get third partied and it is going to feel personal. It is not.\"\n  \"Everyone gets third partied. The good players just get third partied while standing on the box, which is exactly why they win and we do not.\"\nCLOSE:\n  \"That is the guide. Stand on the box. Set it on fire. Subscribe if you are also bad.\"\n\nFOOTAGE NEEDED\nAll of it already exists in the Sep 8 and 9 recordings: whiffs, a cashout hold, the barrel throw, the Citadel thirteen elimination scoreboard, the Fortune Stadium win board showing three eliminations and six deaths. Nothing new has to be captured for this video.",
